   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Sam. Your identity is verified.\n\nHere's what the delivery record shows for order Q-8001 from Burger Barn ($28.03, Visa ending 4242):\n\n- The order was picked up by the courier at 6:47 PM.\n- The courier arrived at the delivery address at 7:05 PM and called you twice, at 7:06 PM and 7:09 PM. Neither call was answered.\n- At 7:15 PM the delivery was marked as failed because the customer was unreachable. The order was returned to the restaurant at 7:28 PM.\n\nThe order was never handed to anyone, so it was not delivered. Because the failure was due to the courier not being able to reach you, I can't issue a refund or credit for this order under our policy.\n\nIf you're still hungry, I can help with other options. If you think the courier's record is wrong, or you have a different address or phone number that should have been used, tell me and I can escalate it to a specialist who can look into it further. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, the courier called me? My phone was on silent because I was in the shower. I only saw the missed calls later. So I just lose my money? That's not fair."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why this is frustrating, and I'm sorry you missed the courier. Being in the shower with your phone on silent is an ordinary situation. But the courier reached the address, called twice, and couldn't get through. Under our policy, a failed delivery because the customer couldn't be reached isn't eligible for a refund or credit, and I'm not able to make an exception.\n\nIf you'd like a person to review your situation, I can pass your case to a human specialist, who will follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise a particular outcome. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, yes, please pass it to someone. I'd like them to take a look at it. I don't really have much else to add, I just want my money back if it's possible."
  },
